    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **System Design** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[Interview] --> N0[Fundamentals]\n  N0 --> N1[Messaging]\n  N1 --> N2[APIs]\n  N2 --> N3[Reliability]\n  N3 --> N4[Data]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Interview question bank System Design 28))\n    Interview\n    Question Bank\n    System Design\n    Accenture\n    Adobe\n    Amazon\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Fundamentals\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Horizontal vs vertical scaling. | Intermediate | Concept | Google, IBM, KPMG, Microsoft |\n| 2 | What is a load balancer and which algorithms do they use? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Deloitte, Microsoft, PwC |\n| 3 | Explain caching strategies: cache-aside, write-through, write-back. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Deloitte, Flipkart, KPMG |\n| 4 | What is a CDN and when does it help? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Deloitte, KPMG, PwC |\n| 5 | Monolith vs microservices: trade-offs. | Intermediate | Concept | Google, IBM, Microsoft, PwC |\n| 6 | Explain database sharding and replication strategies. | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, EY, IBM, Oracle, PwC |\n| 7 | Explain the CAP theorem and eventual consistency. | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Amazon, Capgemini, Flipkart |\n| 8 | What is consistent hashing? | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Amazon, Deloitte, Google, KPMG |\n\n### Messaging\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Why use a message queue? Kafka vs RabbitMQ. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Amazon, EY, KPMG |\n| 2 | Explain exactly-once vs at-least-once delivery. | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Capgemini, Flipkart, IBM, Microsoft |\n\n### APIs\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is an API gateway and what does it handle? | Intermediate | Concept | EY, Google, Microsoft, PwC |\n| 2 | How do you design a rate limiter (token bucket vs sliding window)? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Amazon, IBM, PwC |\n\n### Reliability\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain circuit breaker, retry with backoff and bulkhead patterns. | Advanced | Concept | Capgemini, Deloitte, EY, Flipkart, PwC |\n| 2 | How do you design for high availability and disaster recovery (RPO/RTO)? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Deloitte, EY, Google, PwC |\n\n### Data\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain the Saga pattern for distributed transactions. | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Deloitte, IBM, KPMG, Microsoft |\n| 2 | What is CQRS and event sourcing? | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Deloitte, Flipkart, Google, IBM |\n\n### Design\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design a URL shortener. | Advanced | Design | Accenture, EY, Flipkart, Oracle, PwC |\n| 2 | Design a chat application like WhatsApp. | Advanced | Design | Amazon, Deloitte, Flipkart, IBM, KPMG |\n| 3 | Design a news feed like Instagram or LinkedIn. | Advanced | Design | Accenture, Adobe, Capgemini, Google, KPMG |\n| 4 | Design a video streaming service like YouTube. | Advanced | Design | Capgemini, Deloitte, EY, Flipkart, KPMG |\n| 5 | Design a ride-hailing service like Uber. | Advanced | Design | Accenture, Adobe, Amazon, Microsoft, Oracle |\n| 6 | Design a notification system. | Advanced | Design | Capgemini, Deloitte, IBM, Microsoft, PwC |\n| 7 | Design an e-commerce checkout system. | Advanced | Design | Accenture, Capgemini, KPMG, Oracle, PwC |\n| 8 | Design a distributed test execution platform for 10,000 tests. | Advanced | Design | Accenture, EY, Microsoft, Oracle, PwC |\n\n### Observability\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you design logging, metrics and tracing for microservices? | Advanced | Concept | Capgemini, Deloitte, Google, KPMG, Microsoft |\n\n### Security\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you design authentication and authorization for microservices? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, EY, Flipkart, Microsoft, PwC |\n\n### LLD\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design a parking lot (low-level design with classes). | Intermediate | Design | Accenture, EY, Flipkart, KPMG |\n| 2 | Design an LRU cache. | Advanced | Design | Amazon, Capgemini, Deloitte, Microsoft, Oracle |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
