    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **GenAI & Machine Learning** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[Interview] --> N0[ML basics]\n  N0 --> N1[Deep learning]\n  N1 --> N2[LLMs]\n  N2 --> N3[Prompting]\n  N3 --> N4[RAG]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Interview question bank GenAI Machine Le))\n    Interview\n    Question Bank\n    GenAI Machine Learning\n    Accenture\n    Adobe\n    Amazon\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### ML basics\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Supervised vs unsupervised vs reinforcement learning. | Beginner | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Capgemini, Wipro |\n| 2 | Explain overfitting and underfitting and how to handle them. | Beginner | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, IBM, KPMG |\n| 3 | Explain bias-variance trade-off. | Intermediate | Concept | Deloitte, Flipkart, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | Precision, recall, F1 and when accuracy is misleading. | Intermediate | Concept | EY, Infosys, KPMG, LTIMindtree |\n| 5 | How does a random forest differ from gradient boosting? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Google, Infosys, Microsoft |\n| 6 | What is cross-validation and why use it? | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, Microsoft, PwC |\n\n### Deep learning\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain backpropagation and the role of activation functions. | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Deloitte, KPMG, Oracle |\n| 2 | Explain the transformer architecture and self-attention. | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Deloitte, Oracle, PwC |\n\n### LLMs\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is a large language model and what are tokens? | Beginner | Concept | Amazon, Deloitte, Oracle, TCS |\n| 2 | Explain temperature, top-p and max tokens. | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Flipkart, PwC, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | What causes hallucinations and how do you reduce them? | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, Infosys, TCS |\n| 4 | Fine-tuning vs prompt engineering vs RAG: how do you choose? | Intermediate | Concept | EY, Google, LTIMindtree, Wipro |\n| 5 | Explain LoRA / QLoRA and when parameter-efficient fine-tuning is appropriate. | Advanced | Concept | Google, Infosys, KPMG, PwC, TCS |\n\n### Prompting\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain zero-shot, few-shot and chain-of-thought prompting. | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, Deloitte, LTIMindtree |\n| 2 | What is prompt injection and how do you defend against it? | Advanced | Concept | Amazon, Capgemini, Deloitte, HCLTech, Wipro |\n\n### RAG\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain a RAG pipeline end to end. | Intermediate | Concept | Deloitte, EY, Google, Infosys |\n| 2 | What are embeddings and how does vector similarity search work? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, HCLTech, KPMG, TCS |\n| 3 | How do you choose a chunking strategy? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Flipkart, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n| 4 | How do you evaluate a RAG system (faithfulness, relevance, recall)? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, EY, Microsoft, PwC, Wipro |\n| 5 | Explain hybrid search and re-ranking. | Advanced | Concept | Capgemini, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Oracle, TCS |\n\n### Vector DB\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Compare FAISS, Pinecone, pgvector and Chroma. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Amazon, LTIMindtree, TCS |\n\n### Agents\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is an AI agent and how does tool calling work? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, IBM, KPMG, Wipro |\n| 2 | What is the Model Context Protocol (MCP) and what problem does it solve? | Advanced | Concept | Amazon, Capgemini, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Wipro |\n| 3 | How do you design guardrails for an agent that can take actions? | Advanced | Scenario | Adobe, EY, Google, KPMG, Wipro |\n\n### LLMOps\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you monitor LLM applications in production (cost, latency, quality)? | Advanced | Concept | Amazon, EY, HCLTech, Infosys, Wipro |\n| 2 | How do you version prompts and run regression evals? | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Deloitte, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Oracle |\n| 3 | How would you reduce LLM inference cost by 50% without losing quality? | Advanced | Scenario | Capgemini, Flipkart, IBM, Microsoft, Oracle |\n\n### Frameworks\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | LangChain vs LlamaIndex: strengths of each. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Capgemini, PwC |\n\n### Responsible AI\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What are key responsible AI concerns: bias, privacy, explainability? | Intermediate | Concept | Infosys, KPMG, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Testing AI\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you test a GenAI chatbot before release? | Advanced | Scenario | Amazon, Capgemini, IBM, KPMG, LTIMindtree |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
