    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **Playwright** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAligned with [Playwright Locators](https://playwright.dev/docs/locators): role-first, then test-id contracts, CSS/XPath last.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Need[Need element] --> Prefer[Prefer user-facing]\n  Prefer --> Role[getByRole + name]\n  Prefer --> Text[getByText / Label / Placeholder]\n  Prefer --> Tid[getByTestId contract]\n  Prefer -->|last resort| Css[locator CSS/XPath]\n  Role --> Act[Click / fill / assert]\n  Text --> Act\n  Tid --> Act\n  Css --> Act\n  Act --> Wait[Auto-wait + retry]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Playwright locators))\n    Recommended\n      getByRole\n      getByText\n      getByLabel\n      getByPlaceholder\n      getByAltText\n      getByTitle\n      getByTestId\n    Engine\n      Auto-wait\n      Retry\n      Strict mode\n    Avoid first\n      Brittle CSS\n      Absolute XPath\n```\n\n\n### Basics\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How does Playwright differ from Selenium and Cypress architecturally? | Beginner | Concept | Cognizant, EY, Flipkart, HCLTech |\n| 2 | Explain browser, context and page in Playwright. | Beginner | Concept | Accenture, Flipkart, Google, TCS |\n| 3 | What is auto-waiting and which actions trigger actionability checks? | Beginner | Concept | Amazon, Capgemini, Deloitte, PwC |\n\n### Locators\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Which locators does Playwright recommend (getByRole, getByLabel, getByTestId) and why? | Beginner | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Deloitte, Oracle |\n| 2 | Locator vs ElementHandle: why are locators preferred? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Infosys, KPMG |\n| 3 | How do you filter and chain locators, e.g. a row containing specific text? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Cognizant, Infosys, KPMG |\n| 4 | What does strict mode mean for locators? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, IBM, Infosys, Wipro |\n\n### Assertions\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Web-first assertions: how does expect(locator).toHaveText retry? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, Deloitte, PwC, Wipro |\n| 2 | Soft assertions vs hard assertions; when to use each. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, IBM, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | How do visual comparisons (toHaveScreenshot) work and what makes them flaky? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Deloitte, HCLTech, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Test runner\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain fixtures and how to create a custom fixture. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, Microsoft, TCS |\n| 2 | How do projects in playwright.config enable cross-browser runs? | Intermediate | Concept | Flipkart, Google, IBM, Infosys |\n| 3 | How do you configure retries, timeouts and parallel workers? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, HCLTech, Infosys, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | test.describe.serial vs parallel mode: trade-offs. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, EY, HCLTech, Oracle |\n\n### Auth\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you reuse login state with storageState? | Intermediate | Concept | LTIMindtree, Microsoft, TCS, Wipro |\n| 2 | How do you handle multiple user roles in the same test run? | Advanced | Scenario | Adobe, HCLTech, Microsoft, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Network\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you intercept and mock API responses with page.route? | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Google, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | How do you wait for a specific network response? | Intermediate | Concept | EY, Google, Infosys, PwC |\n\n### API testing\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you use the request fixture for API testing? | Intermediate | Concept | Google, IBM, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | How do you combine API setup with UI verification in one test? | Advanced | Scenario | Flipkart, HCLTech, Microsoft, PwC, Wipro |\n\n### Debugging\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you use Trace Viewer, UI mode and the inspector? | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Google, PwC, TCS |\n| 2 | What does codegen generate and why should you refactor its output? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Amazon, IBM, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Advanced\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you handle iframes, new tabs and popups? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, Deloitte, IBM, KPMG |\n| 2 | How do you handle file uploads and downloads? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, Flipkart, Infosys, TCS |\n| 3 | How do you run Playwright tests with sharding in CI? | Advanced | Concept | EY, Google, IBM, Microsoft, TCS |\n| 4 | Your suite is flaky only in CI. How do you diagnose it? | Advanced | Scenario | Capgemini, Flipkart, Infosys, KPMG, TCS |\n| 5 | How do you structure a Page Object Model in Playwright with TypeScript? | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Deloitte, EY, Google, KPMG |\n| 6 | How do you emulate devices, geolocation, timezone and permissions? | Advanced | Concept | Cognizant, EY, Flipkart, LTIMindtree, Microsoft |\n\n### CI/CD\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you run Playwright in GitHub Actions and publish the HTML report? | Intermediate | Concept | Deloitte, EY, Google, Oracle |\n| 2 | How do you run Playwright in Docker and why use the official image? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Deloitte, Flipkart, HCLTech, LTIMindtree |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
