    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **Selenium & Automation Frameworks** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAligned with [Playwright Locators](https://playwright.dev/docs/locators): role-first, then test-id contracts, CSS/XPath last.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Need[Need element] --> Prefer[Prefer user-facing]\n  Prefer --> Role[getByRole + name]\n  Prefer --> Text[getByText / Label / Placeholder]\n  Prefer --> Tid[getByTestId contract]\n  Prefer -->|last resort| Css[locator CSS/XPath]\n  Role --> Act[Click / fill / assert]\n  Text --> Act\n  Tid --> Act\n  Css --> Act\n  Act --> Wait[Auto-wait + retry]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Playwright locators))\n    Recommended\n      getByRole\n      getByText\n      getByLabel\n      getByPlaceholder\n      getByAltText\n      getByTitle\n      getByTestId\n    Engine\n      Auto-wait\n      Retry\n      Strict mode\n    Avoid first\n      Brittle CSS\n      Absolute XPath\n```\n\n\n### Selenium basics\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain Selenium WebDriver architecture and how the browser driver communicates. | Beginner | Concept | Cognizant, HCLTech, IBM, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | What locator strategies exist and which order do you prefer and why? | Beginner | Concept | Cognizant, PwC, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | findElement vs findElements: behaviour when nothing is found. | Beginner | Concept | Deloitte, EY, LTIMindtree, TCS |\n| 4 | Implicit vs explicit vs fluent wait; why should you not mix them? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, Deloitte, EY, Wipro |\n| 5 | How do you handle StaleElementReferenceException? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, LTIMindtree, PwC, Tech Mahindra |\n| 6 | How do you handle alerts, frames and multiple windows? | Intermediate | Concept | EY, HCLTech, Infosys, LTIMindtree |\n| 7 | Write a dynamic XPath for a table cell based on a row label. | Intermediate | Coding | Capgemini, EY, PwC, TCS |\n| 8 | How do you handle dropdowns, both native select and custom? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Cognizant, EY, IBM |\n| 9 | How do you perform mouse hover, drag and drop and right-click? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, EY, Infosys, Wipro |\n| 10 | How do you take screenshots on failure automatically? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, EY, Infosys, PwC |\n| 11 | How do you handle file upload and download in Selenium? | Advanced | Concept | Deloitte, HCLTech, IBM, KPMG, LTIMindtree |\n| 12 | What is JavaScriptExecutor used for and when is it a smell? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Cognizant, Deloitte, PwC, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Framework design\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain the Page Object Model and Page Factory. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Cognizant, EY, KPMG |\n| 2 | Explain the folder structure of your current automation framework. | Intermediate | Concept | Deloitte, HCLTech, Infosys, TCS |\n| 3 | How do you design a hybrid framework (data-driven plus keyword-driven)? | Advanced | Concept | Deloitte, EY, HCLTech, KPMG, PwC |\n| 4 | How do you manage environment configuration and test data? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Cognizant, Deloitte, IBM, LTIMindtree |\n| 5 | How do you reduce flaky tests in a large suite? | Advanced | Scenario | Accenture, IBM, LTIMindtree, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n\n### TestNG/JUnit\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain TestNG annotations and their execution order. | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Cognizant, TCS, Wipro |\n| 2 | How do you run tests in parallel with TestNG and what can break? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, IBM, PwC, Wipro |\n| 3 | What are DataProviders and how do you feed Excel data into tests? | Intermediate | Concept | EY, IBM, LTIMindtree, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | How do you rerun only failed tests? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, EY, HCLTech, TCS |\n\n### BDD\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain Cucumber: feature files, step definitions and hooks. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, IBM, KPMG, Wipro |\n| 2 | Scenario vs Scenario Outline; how do tags help? | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, LTIMindtree, PwC, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | How do you keep step definitions reusable and avoid duplication? | Advanced | Scenario | Capgemini, EY, KPMG, PwC, TCS |\n\n### Grid & CI\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is Selenium Grid and how does it scale execution? | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, IBM, KPMG, PwC |\n| 2 | How do you run your suite in Jenkins or Azure DevOps with reports? | Advanced | Concept | Deloitte, IBM, PwC, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | How do you run tests in Docker containers? | Advanced | Concept | Capgemini, Infosys, LTIMindtree, PwC, Wipro |\n\n### Reporting\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you generate Extent or Allure reports? | Intermediate | Concept | KPMG, LTIMindtree, PwC, TCS |\n\n### Selenium 4\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is new in Selenium 4: relative locators, CDP and W3C protocol? | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Deloitte, TCS, Wipro |\n\n### Strategy\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Which test cases should not be automated and why? | Advanced | Scenario | Accenture, Capgemini, Infosys, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
