    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **JavaScript** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[Interview] --> N0[Basics]\n  N0 --> N1[Functions]\n  N1 --> N2[this prototypes]\n  N2 --> N3[Async]\n  N3 --> N4[Coding]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Interview question bank JavaScript 32 qu))\n    Interview\n    Question Bank\n    JavaScript\n    Accenture\n    Adobe\n    Amazon\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Basics\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Difference between var, let and const, including hoisting and TDZ. | Beginner | Concept | Accenture, HCLTech, TCS, Wipro |\n| 2 | Difference between == and ===; list surprising coercion cases. | Beginner | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, HCLTech, LTIMindtree |\n| 3 | What are primitive vs reference types in JavaScript? | Beginner | Concept | Accenture, Amazon, Google, Wipro |\n| 4 | Explain null vs undefined vs undeclared. | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, Flipkart, Google, TCS |\n\n### Functions\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is a closure? Give a practical use such as data privacy or memoization. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Flipkart, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | Arrow functions vs regular functions: this, arguments and constructors. | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Google, LTIMindtree, Oracle |\n| 3 | Explain call, apply and bind with examples. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, HCLTech, Infosys, Oracle |\n| 4 | What is currying and how do you implement it? | Intermediate | Concept | Google, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Wipro |\n\n### this & prototypes\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How is the value of this determined in different call sites? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, Google, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | Explain prototypal inheritance and how class syntax maps to it. | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Capgemini, Flipkart, LTIMindtree, Microsoft |\n\n### Async\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain the event loop, call stack, microtask and macrotask queues. | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, Flipkart, HCLTech |\n| 2 | Promises vs async/await: how do you handle errors in each? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Flipkart, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | Promise.all vs allSettled vs race vs any. | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, HCLTech, Microsoft, Oracle |\n| 4 | Predict the output order of setTimeout, Promise.then and console.log. | Advanced | Coding | HCLTech, Infosys, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Wipro |\n| 5 | Implement a retry wrapper with exponential backoff for an async function. | Advanced | Coding | Adobe, Cognizant, Infosys, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Coding\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Remove duplicates from an array in three different ways. | Beginner | Coding | Adobe, HCLTech, LTIMindtree, Wipro |\n| 2 | Flatten a deeply nested array without using flat(). | Intermediate | Coding | Capgemini, Flipkart, Google, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | Implement debounce and throttle. | Intermediate | Coding | Accenture, LTIMindtree, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n| 4 | Deep clone an object; discuss structuredClone vs JSON approach. | Intermediate | Coding | Accenture, Capgemini, Microsoft, TCS |\n| 5 | Implement your own Promise.all. | Advanced | Coding | Accenture, Cognizant, Flipkart, Oracle, TCS |\n| 6 | Implement Array.prototype.map and reduce polyfills. | Advanced | Coding | Accenture, Adobe, Capgemini, Cognizant, TCS |\n\n### DOM\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain event bubbling, capturing and delegation. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Flipkart, Google |\n| 2 | What causes reflow and repaint and how do you minimise them? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, Google, HCLTech |\n\n### ES6+\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain destructuring, spread and rest operators. | Beginner | Concept | Amazon, Capgemini, Microsoft, Oracle |\n| 2 | Map vs Object and Set vs Array: when to use each. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Capgemini, Infosys, Oracle |\n| 3 | What are ES modules and how do they differ from CommonJS? | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Google, Microsoft, Wipro |\n\n### Browser\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | localStorage vs sessionStorage vs cookies, including security concerns. | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Microsoft, Oracle, TCS |\n| 2 | Explain CORS and why preflight requests happen. | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, Google, Infosys, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Security\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How do you prevent XSS in a front-end application? | Advanced | Concept | Capgemini, Cognizant, Flipkart, Google, Oracle |\n\n### Node.js\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How is Node.js single-threaded yet able to handle concurrency? | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Flipkart, Microsoft, Oracle |\n| 2 | Explain streams in Node.js and when you would use them. | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Google, Infosys, LTIMindtree, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### TypeScript\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | interface vs type in TypeScript; when does it matter? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Cognizant, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
