    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **Data Structures & Algorithms** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[Interview] --> N0[Arrays]\n  N0 --> N1[Strings]\n  N1 --> N2[Hashing]\n  N2 --> N3[Linked List]\n  N3 --> N4[Stack Queue]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Interview question bank Data Structures ))\n    Interview\n    Question Bank\n    Data Structures Algorith\n    Accenture\n    Adobe\n    Amazon\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Arrays\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Find the maximum and minimum in an array in a single pass. | Beginner | Coding | Flipkart, HCLTech, Oracle, Wipro |\n| 2 | Move all zeros to the end while keeping the order of other elements. | Beginner | Coding | Accenture, Amazon, Capgemini, Wipro |\n| 3 | Find the maximum subarray sum (Kadane's algorithm). | Intermediate | Coding | Cognizant, Google, Infosys, Wipro |\n| 4 | Two Sum: return indices of two numbers adding up to a target. | Intermediate | Coding | Adobe, Amazon, Google, TCS |\n| 5 | Rotate an array by k positions in place. | Intermediate | Coding | Accenture, Capgemini, Google, Microsoft |\n| 6 | Trapping rain water: compute total water trapped. | Advanced | Coding | Amazon, HCLTech, Microsoft, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Strings\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Check whether two strings are anagrams. | Beginner | Coding | Adobe, HCLTech, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | Longest substring without repeating characters. | Intermediate | Coding | Accenture, Google, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | Check if a string of brackets is balanced. | Intermediate | Coding | Flipkart, TCS, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n| 4 | Longest palindromic substring. | Advanced | Coding | Amazon, Cognizant, Infosys, LTIMindtree, Microsoft |\n\n### Hashing\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Group anagrams from a list of words. | Intermediate | Coding | Flipkart, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Wipro |\n| 2 | Find the longest consecutive sequence in an unsorted array. | Intermediate | Coding | Adobe, Cognizant, Google, HCLTech |\n\n### Linked List\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Reverse a singly linked list iteratively and recursively. | Beginner | Coding | Flipkart, Google, Oracle, TCS |\n| 2 | Detect a cycle in a linked list and find its start node. | Intermediate | Coding | Infosys, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, TCS |\n| 3 | Merge two sorted linked lists. | Intermediate | Coding | Amazon, Cognizant, LTIMindtree, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | Find the middle node of a linked list in one pass. | Intermediate | Coding | Adobe, HCLTech, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Stack & Queue\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Implement a queue using two stacks. | Intermediate | Coding | Cognizant, HCLTech, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n| 2 | Next greater element for each element of an array. | Intermediate | Coding | Adobe, Cognizant, Infosys, TCS |\n| 3 | Design a min-stack with O(1) getMin. | Advanced | Coding | Cognizant, Flipkart, Google, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Trees\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Level-order traversal of a binary tree. | Intermediate | Coding | Accenture, Flipkart, Infosys, Microsoft |\n| 2 | Find the height and check if a binary tree is balanced. | Intermediate | Coding | Amazon, Infosys, LTIMindtree, Microsoft |\n| 3 | Validate a binary search tree. | Intermediate | Coding | Amazon, Capgemini, Google, Microsoft |\n| 4 | Lowest common ancestor of two nodes in a binary tree. | Advanced | Coding | Accenture, Amazon, Capgemini, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n\n### Graphs\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BFS vs DFS: implement both and explain use cases. | Intermediate | Coding | Accenture, Infosys, LTIMindtree, Oracle |\n| 2 | Number of islands in a 2D grid. | Advanced | Coding | Adobe, Infosys, Oracle, TCS, Wipro |\n| 3 | Detect a cycle in a directed graph; apply topological sort. | Advanced | Coding | Accenture, Cognizant, HCLTech, LTIMindtree, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | Explain Dijkstra's algorithm and its limitations with negative weights. | Advanced | Concept | Amazon, Infosys, Microsoft, Oracle, TCS |\n\n### Sorting & Searching\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Implement binary search and state its complexity. | Beginner | Coding | Flipkart, Infosys, LTIMindtree, Wipro |\n| 2 | Compare quicksort and merge sort: stability, space and worst case. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Capgemini, Google, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | Search in a rotated sorted array. | Intermediate | Coding | Amazon, Google, Oracle, Wipro |\n\n### Dynamic Programming\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Climbing stairs / Fibonacci with memoization and tabulation. | Intermediate | Coding | Accenture, Adobe, Flipkart, Infosys |\n| 2 | Longest common subsequence of two strings. | Advanced | Coding | Amazon, Capgemini, Flipkart, Google, Infosys |\n| 3 | 0/1 knapsack problem. | Advanced | Coding | Adobe, Flipkart, LTIMindtree, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | Coin change: minimum coins to make an amount. | Advanced | Coding | Accenture, Adobe, Google, Microsoft, Wipro |\n\n### Complexity\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain Big-O and the complexity of common operations on arrays, maps and trees. | Beginner | Concept | Amazon, Capgemini, HCLTech, Tech Mahindra |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
