    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **SQL & Databases** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[Interview] --> N0[Basics]\n  N0 --> N1[Queries]\n  N1 --> N2[Window functions]\n  N2 --> N3[CTEs]\n  N3 --> N4[Indexes]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Interview question bank SQL Databases 32))\n    Interview\n    Question Bank\n    SQL Databases\n    Accenture\n    Adobe\n    Amazon\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Basics\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Difference between DELETE, TRUNCATE and DROP. | Beginner | Concept | Cognizant, Google, HCLTech, Microsoft |\n| 2 | Difference between WHERE and HAVING. | Beginner | Concept | Adobe, Deloitte, EY, Google |\n| 3 | Explain primary key, unique key and foreign key. | Beginner | Concept | KPMG, Microsoft, Oracle, TCS |\n| 4 | What are the different types of JOINs? Draw the result for each. | Beginner | Concept | Amazon, Capgemini, KPMG, Microsoft |\n| 5 | UNION vs UNION ALL: performance and result differences. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Deloitte, IBM, KPMG |\n\n### Queries\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Find the second highest salary from an Employee table. | Beginner | Coding | Adobe, Google, LTIMindtree, Wipro |\n| 2 | Find the Nth highest salary without using LIMIT/TOP. | Intermediate | Coding | EY, Flipkart, Google, PwC |\n| 3 | Find duplicate records in a table and delete all but one. | Intermediate | Coding | Adobe, Amazon, Cognizant, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | List employees who earn more than their manager. | Intermediate | Coding | Adobe, Amazon, Capgemini, Deloitte |\n| 5 | Find departments with no employees. | Intermediate | Coding | Deloitte, IBM, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 6 | Get the highest paid employee in each department. | Intermediate | Coding | Adobe, Google, LTIMindtree, Oracle |\n| 7 | Calculate a running total of sales by date. | Advanced | Coding | Amazon, IBM, Infosys, Microsoft, Oracle |\n| 8 | Find customers who ordered in three consecutive months. | Advanced | Coding | Adobe, Cognizant, IBM, KPMG, LTIMindtree |\n\n### Window functions\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain ROW_NUMBER, RANK and DENSE_RANK with an example. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, HCLTech, KPMG |\n| 2 | Use LAG/LEAD to compute month-over-month revenue change. | Advanced | Coding | EY, HCLTech, IBM, LTIMindtree, Oracle |\n| 3 | What does PARTITION BY do and how is it different from GROUP BY? | Advanced | Concept | Cognizant, Flipkart, Google, Oracle, Wipro |\n\n### CTEs\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is a CTE and when is it better than a subquery? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Flipkart, HCLTech, LTIMindtree |\n| 2 | Write a recursive CTE to display an employee-manager hierarchy. | Advanced | Coding | Adobe, Cognizant, IBM, Oracle, Wipro |\n\n### Indexes\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Clustered vs non-clustered index: how does each store data? | Intermediate | Concept | EY, Flipkart, Google, IBM |\n| 2 | When can an index make a query slower? | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Google, KPMG, LTIMindtree, Microsoft |\n| 3 | A query that ran in 2 seconds now takes 2 minutes. How do you diagnose it? | Advanced | Scenario | Flipkart, Google, Infosys, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Normalization\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain 1NF, 2NF, 3NF and when denormalization is justified. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Amazon, Capgemini, EY |\n\n### Transactions\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain ACID properties with a banking example. | Intermediate | Concept | Flipkart, HCLTech, IBM, PwC |\n| 2 | Explain isolation levels and the anomalies each prevents. | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, EY, IBM, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | What are deadlocks in databases and how do you prevent them? | Advanced | Concept | Amazon, KPMG, Oracle, PwC, TCS |\n\n### Objects\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Stored procedure vs function: differences and use cases. | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | What are views and materialized views? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, Google, TCS |\n| 3 | What are triggers and what are the risks of overusing them? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, EY, Infosys, Wipro |\n\n### NoSQL\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | SQL vs NoSQL: how do you choose for a new project? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Capgemini, HCLTech, Oracle |\n| 2 | Explain the CAP theorem and where MongoDB and Cassandra sit. | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, KPMG, LTIMindtree, TCS |\n\n### Data warehousing\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Star schema vs snowflake schema; fact vs dimension tables. | Advanced | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, EY, Oracle, Wipro |\n| 2 | Explain slowly changing dimensions Type 1, 2 and 3. | Advanced | Concept | Capgemini, Infosys, PwC, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
