    "content": "## Scope\nQuestion-only bank for **Java & OOP** interviews. Use it as a checklist: answer each out loud, then mark weak areas.\n\n- **Levels:** Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced\n- **Types:** Concept, Coding, Scenario, Design, Behavioural\n- **Companies:** indicative of where the topic is commonly tested — search the site for a company name (e.g. \"TCS\") to filter across all skills.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[Interview] --> N0[OOP]\n  N0 --> N1[Core Java]\n  N1 --> N2[Collections]\n  N2 --> N3[Java 8+]\n  N3 --> N4[Multithreading]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Interview question bank Java OOP 35 ques))\n    Interview\n    Question Bank\n    Java OOP\n    Accenture\n    Adobe\n    Amazon\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### OOP\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain the four pillars of OOP with a real example from a project you worked on. | Beginner | Concept | Adobe, Infosys, TCS, Wipro |\n| 2 | What is the difference between an abstract class and an interface in Java 8+? | Beginner | Concept | Flipkart, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | When would you prefer composition over inheritance? Give a concrete case. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Amazon, HCLTech, Wipro |\n| 4 | Explain method overloading vs overriding, including rules on return types and access modifiers. | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Flipkart, LTIMindtree, Microsoft |\n\n### Core Java\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Why is String immutable in Java and what are the benefits? | Beginner | Concept | Cognizant, Google, Infosys, Tech Mahindra |\n| 2 | Difference between ==, equals() and hashCode(); what breaks if you override only one? | Beginner | Concept | Google, HCLTech, Infosys, TCS |\n| 3 | Explain the contract between equals() and hashCode() when using objects as HashMap keys. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Microsoft, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | What are checked vs unchecked exceptions and how do you design a custom exception hierarchy? | Intermediate | Concept | Google, HCLTech, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n| 5 | Explain final, finally and finalize with examples. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, LTIMindtree, Microsoft, Wipro |\n| 6 | What is the difference between String, StringBuilder and StringBuffer? | Beginner | Concept | Adobe, Capgemini, Google, HCLTech |\n\n### Collections\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How does HashMap work internally, including hashing, buckets, collisions and treeification? | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Cognizant, Oracle, TCS |\n| 2 | ArrayList vs LinkedList: which operations favour each and why? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Capgemini, HCLTech, TCS |\n| 3 | What is the difference between fail-fast and fail-safe iterators? | Intermediate | Concept | HCLTech, LTIMindtree, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n| 4 | How does ConcurrentHashMap achieve thread safety without locking the whole map? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Capgemini, LTIMindtree, Oracle, Wipro |\n| 5 | Write code to remove duplicates from a List while preserving insertion order. | Beginner | Coding | Adobe, Flipkart, Google, LTIMindtree |\n| 6 | Sort a list of Employee objects by salary descending, then by name, using Comparator. | Intermediate | Coding | Amazon, HCLTech, LTIMindtree, Wipro |\n\n### Java 8+\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain Streams: intermediate vs terminal operations and lazy evaluation. | Intermediate | Concept | Adobe, Microsoft, TCS, Wipro |\n| 2 | Using streams, group employees by department and compute average salary per department. | Intermediate | Coding | Flipkart, Google, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 3 | What is Optional and what are common misuses of it? | Intermediate | Concept | HCLTech, Infosys, Oracle, Wipro |\n| 4 | What are functional interfaces? Name four built-in ones and their use. | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Cognizant, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n| 5 | Explain map vs flatMap with an example of nested collections. | Advanced | Concept | Adobe, Infosys, Oracle, TCS, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Multithreading\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Thread vs Runnable vs Callable: when do you use each? | Intermediate | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, Flipkart, HCLTech |\n| 2 | Explain synchronized, volatile and the happens-before relationship. | Intermediate | Concept | Cognizant, Infosys, Microsoft, TCS |\n| 3 | How does ExecutorService manage thread pools and how do you size one? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Amazon, Flipkart, Wipro |\n| 4 | How would you detect and fix a deadlock in a production Java service? | Advanced | Scenario | Accenture, Capgemini, Infosys, Microsoft, Tech Mahindra |\n| 5 | What is CompletableFuture and how do you chain async tasks with error handling? | Advanced | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Infosys, LTIMindtree, Oracle |\n\n### JVM\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Explain JVM memory areas: heap, stack, metaspace and what lives where. | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Cognizant, Google, Wipro |\n| 2 | How does garbage collection work? Compare G1 with ZGC at a high level. | Advanced | Concept | Amazon, Cognizant, Infosys, Oracle, Wipro |\n| 3 | An application throws OutOfMemoryError after a few hours. How do you investigate? | Advanced | Scenario | Adobe, Capgemini, Oracle, Tech Mahindra, Wipro |\n\n### Design Patterns\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Implement a thread-safe Singleton and explain double-checked locking. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Amazon, Oracle, TCS |\n| 2 | Explain Factory and Builder patterns and where you have used them. | Intermediate | Concept | Capgemini, Cognizant, Google, TCS |\n| 3 | Explain SOLID principles with one violation and its fix for each. | Advanced | Concept | Cognizant, Infosys, Microsoft, Oracle, Tech Mahindra |\n\n### Spring Boot\n\n| # | Question | Level | Type | Commonly asked at |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | What is dependency injection and how does Spring manage bean lifecycle and scopes? | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Amazon, Capgemini, Microsoft |\n| 2 | Explain @Component, @Service, @Repository and @Controller differences. | Intermediate | Concept | Accenture, Adobe, Google, Oracle |\n| 3 | How do you handle global exceptions and validation in a Spring Boot REST API? | Advanced | Scenario | Amazon, Google, Microsoft, TCS, Wipro |\n\n## How to practise\n1. Pick one subtopic per day.\n2. Answer in 60–90 seconds; write code for Coding rows.\n3. Revisit Advanced rows before product-company or architect rounds.\n",
