    "content": "## Core idea\nAPI testing with Playwright shows up constantly in production work. This lesson turns the official docs outline into a practical mental model you can reuse in interviews and day-to-day coding.\n\nContext signal from docs: Introduction\n\n\n\n\n## Visual overview\nFrom [Fixtures](https://playwright.dev/docs/test-fixtures): declare deps in test args — runner isolates setup/teardown.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Worker[Worker process] --> WFix[Worker fixtures]\n  WFix --> File[Test file]\n  File --> TFix[Test fixtures page/context/request]\n  TFix --> Body[Test body]\n  Body --> Down[Fixture teardown]\n  Hook[beforeEach / afterEach] --> Body\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Fixtures))\n    Built-in\n      page\n      context\n      browser\n      request\n    Custom\n      test.extend\n      auto fixtures\n    Hooks\n      beforeEach\n      afterEach\n      beforeAll\n      afterAll\n    Isolation\n      Per-test context\n      Worker reuse\n```\n\n\n## Practical rules\n- Build intuition around: Introduction​\n- Build intuition around: Writing API Test​\n- Build intuition around: Configuration​\n- Build intuition around: Writing tests​\n- Build intuition around: Setup and teardown​\n- Prefer clear names and small examples over memorizing every API edge case.\n- Verify behavior with a tiny snippet before wiring it into a large suite.\n\n## Try this\n```js\nimport { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';export default defineConfig({ use: { // All requests we send go to this API endpoint. baseURL: 'https://api.github.com', extraHTTPHeaders: { // We set this header per GitHub guidelines. 'Accept': 'application/vnd.github.v3+json', //\n```\n\n## Quick quiz\nQ: What is the first thing you should clarify about API testing with Playwright?\nA: The exact problem it solves and the smallest example that proves you understand it.\n\n## Key takeaway\nMaster API testing with Playwright by explaining it out loud, writing one minimal example, and only then reading deeper docs sections.\n\nFurther reading: https://playwright.dev/docs/api-testing\n",
